{"url": "https://www.polito.it/en/education/phd-programmes-and-postgraduate-school/admissions-to-phd-programmes/international-students/admission-process", "final_url": "https://www.polito.it/en/education/phd-programmes-and-postgraduate-school/admissions-to-phd-programmes/international-students/admission-process", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "Admission process | Politecnico di Torino\nSkip to main content\nServices Status\nHeader\nLogin\nEN\nIT\nToggle language menu\nSkip to main content\nNavigazione principale\nPoliTO\nPoliTO\nToggle submenu\nPolitecnico di Torino\nGo to page PoliTO\nAbout us\nPolitecnico at a glance\nStrategy\nAn international University\nEquity, welfare and inclusion\nSustainable campus\nCareer Hub\nWork with us\nQuality\nCommunication and press office\nDonations\nEducation\nEducation\nToggle submenu\nEducation\nGo to page Education\nApplying, studying, graduating\nBachelor's degree programmes\nMaster's degree programmes\nPh.D. programmes and Postgraduate School\nSpecializing Master's programmes and lifelong learning\nInternational students\nServices and life at Politecnico\nPoliTO+ Learning Experiences\nTeaching Lab\nQuality of education\nResearch\nResearch\nToggle submenu\nResearch\nGo to page Research\nScenario\nEcosystem\nResearch funding\nResults\nPrinciples and policies\nEvents and opportunities\nOrizzonti\nWorking in research\nQualit\u00e0 della ricerca\nInnovation\nInnovation\nToggle submenu\nInnovation\nGo to page Innovation\nTechnology Transfer System\nCorporate relations\nConnecting research to the market\nEntrepreneurship training\nQualit\u00e0 della Terza Missione\nSocial impact\nSocial impact\nToggle submenu\nSocial impact\nGo to page Social impact\nPoliTO per il Sociale\n2030 Agenda\nCulture\nBiennale Tecnologia\nPoliTO libraries\nPrometeo - Tech Cultures\nTheseus Center\nMasterplan\nQualit\u00e0 della Terza Missione\nSearch\nSearch\nInformation for\nInfo for\nProspective students\nStudents\nInternational students\nGraduates\nPhD candidates\nProfessors and researchers\nStaff\nInstitutions and companies\nHeader\nLogin\nEN\nIT\nToggle language menu\nSearch\nPh.D. programmes and Postgraduate School\nSkip to main content\nDoctoral School\nPh.D. programmes\nAdmissions to Ph.D. programmes\nInternazionalization\nPh.D. path\nPh.D.s and Companies\nNews and calls\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nEducation\nPh.D. programmes and Postgraduate School\nAdmissions to Ph.D. programmes\nInternational students\nAdmission process\nAdmission process\nImmagine\nInternational students compete for positions and scholarships with the same terms and rules of Italian applicants. Candidates who earned their degree abroad are admitted in a Ph.D. programme only if they have a Master's degree (i.e. 2nd level qualification, as defined in the Bologna process) issued by an officially recognised academic institution and granting admission in a Ph.D. programme in the country where the degree was awarded.\nCandidates holding a Master of Science degree obtained abroad must submit the following documents in order for the University Committee to assess the eligibility of the degree for admission to the doctoral program:\nBachelor's degree diploma (EQF level 6);\nCertificate with all the exams taken in the Bachelor\u2019s degree programme (front and back scan) or a document issued by the University including all the exams taken;\nMaster\u2019s degree diploma (EQF level 7). If the official diploma is not available yet, a provisional one can be accepted. Otherwise, it is necessary an official document the specifies the expected date of graduation;\nCertificate with all the exams taken in the Master\u2019s degree programme (front and back scan). If at the final year of programme, a certificate of the exams taken - as updated as possible - with the average of final or current grades;\nDiploma Supplement, if available;\nDeclaration of value or Statement of Comparability issued by the Italian ENIC-NARIC \u2013 CIMEA, if available.\nOnly the candidates who have attended a 1st or 2nd level degree course (totally or in part) at a non-European University are required to include a short explanation on the evaluation system (minimum and maximum grade for passing each exam, final grade, medium average) and the credit system to which it refers. In the event that this information is not present in the document, it is necessary to provide and attach an official statement issued by University that includes the missing information.\nThese documents must be:\nissued by the University in one of the following languages: Italian, English, French or Spanish.\non headed paper with the stamp of the Institution that issued them and the signature of the administrator in charge.\nelectronically signed;\nverifiable online via QR code or verification link.\nApplicants who have already obtained a declaration of conformity issued by an Italian university can just attach a self-certificate to the application form.\nThese documents shall be attached to the application form on the Apply@polito platform by the deadline established in the Call for Applications for admissions.\nIt is understood that candidates with qualifications obtained abroad must meet all the requirements specified in article 6 of the Call for Applications.\nNavigate this section\nDoctoral School\nPh.D. programmes\nAdmissions to Ph.D. programmes\nInternational students\nAdmission process\nIncoming co-tutelle thesis\nBefore leaving\nArrival in Italy\nAdmissions\nCall for applications\nCall for applications CSC\nCall for applications conflict zones\nPh.D. scholarships\nProcedure and requirements for admission\nEvaluation of applicants\nInterview\nResults and ranking lists\nArchive of past Calls for Applications\nEnrolment\nReserving one's Ph.D. position\nEnrolling\nReserved positions\nTransfers from other universities\nInternazionalization\nPh.D. path\nPh.D.s and Companies\nNews and calls\nSince 1859 our students have been changing the world. Support their idea of the future.\nDonate\nSkip to next section\nPi\u00e8 di pagina\nContact\nMaps\nEmergency\nPrivacy policy\nOpen competitions and selections\nCalls for tenders\nIT services\nAlumni\nSign up for PoliTO newsletter\nAdministration Transparency\nAlbo online\nAtti di notifica\nDichiarazione di accessibilit\u00e0\nCookie settings\nPolitecnico di Torino | Corso Duca degli Abruzzi, 24 | 10129 Torino, ITALY | P.IVA/C.F. 00518460019 | PEC politecnicoditorino@pec.polito.it\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedin\nFacebook\nTiktok\nX-Twitter\nYoutube\nTelegram\nThreads\nWechat\nOndeQuadre", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.polito.it/en/education/phd-programmes-and-postgraduate-school/admissions-to-phd-programmes/international-students/admission-process#main-content"], ["Services Status", "https://status.polito.it/"], ["Login", "https://idp.polito.it/home"], ["IT", "https://www.polito.it/didattica/dottorato-di-ricerca-e-scuola-di-specializzazione/ammissione-al-dottorato/studenti-internazionali/modalita-di-accesso"], ["", "https://www.polito.it/en"], ["Skip to main content", "https://www.polito.it/en/education/phd-programmes-and-postgraduate-school/admissions-to-phd-programmes/international-students/admission-process#main-content"], ["PoliTO", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito"], ["Go to page PoliTO", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito"], ["About us", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/about-us"], ["Politecnico at a glance", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/politecnico-at-a-glance"], ["Strategy", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/strategy"], ["An international University", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/an-international-university"], ["Equity, welfare and inclusion", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/equity-welfare-and-inclusion"], ["Sustainable campus", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/sustainable-campus"], ["Career Hub", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/career-hub"], ["Work with us", "https://www.polito.it/en/polito/work-with-us"], ["Quality", "https://www